  "steps": [
    "To a pot on medium heat, add 3 cups of water. Add 1 tbsp salt, 2 cardamom pods, 4 cloves, 1 bay leaf, 1 tbsp chopped coriander stems, 1 slit green chilli, ¼ tsp garam masala, 60g raw soya chunks, Let it boil for 2 minutes.",
    "Now add 400g washed basmati rice to the boiling water.",
    "Once the rice is almost cooked through, add: ¼ cup chopped carrots, ¼ cup green peas, ¼ cup sweet corn.",
    "Let everything continue boiling.",
    "Now bring the flame to low, cover, and let it cook for 10 minutes until the rice is fully cooked.",
    "Once done, set it aside.",
    "Next, to a pan on medium heat, add: 1 tbsp ghee, 1 tsp butter.",
    "Arrange 3 halved tomatoes in the pan like petals of a flower.",
    "Right in the centre, add: 1 chopped onion, 12 garlic cloves, 1 chopped green chilli, ½ tsp salt.",
    "Cover and cook for 5 minutes until the tomatoes soften.",
    "Now remove the tomato skins and mash everything together into a nice chutney.",
    "Add: 1 tsp Kashmiri red chilli powder, ½ tsp turmeric powder.",
    "Mix everything really well.",
    "Now top it with the cooked spiced soya rice.",
    "Sprinkle ½ tsp garam masala over it and give everything one final mix until the rice is nicely coated in that garlic tomato masala.",
    "And your Street-Style Garlic Soya Rice is ready to serve!"
  ],
